# caveshtml

Browser port of Chris Busch’s TI-85 game **Caves** (CENGINE v5 + LVL programs).

## Layout

- `asm/` — original Z80 (CENGINE, actors, sprites, macros). Reference, not rewrite-in-place.
- `levels/` — original ASCII level packs (`.LVL`). Parser/format must match these files.
- Web app files (HTML/JS/CSS) — add here as the port grows.
- `.cursor/plans/` — product, architecture, roadmap, decisions. User edits these; agent must not ignore them.

## Working rules

- Prefer faithful gameplay (physics, tiles, keys, scoring) over “modernizing” unless `plans/decisions.md` records it.
- Do not invent missing compiler/level-handler source; infer from `asm/` + `.LVL` samples.
- Keep changes scoped. Update the relevant plan file when you lock a design choice.
